<newsitem itemid="432735" id="root" date="1997-03-11" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Mutual &amp; Federal ups interim shr, div.</title>
<headline>Mutual &amp; Federal ups interim shr, div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half yr ended December 31, 1996</p>
<p>		(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		    62.7    vs    52.1</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		    12.0    vs    10.0</p>
<p>    Net income		  149.6    vs    123.4</p>
<p>    Net premium income	975.6    vs    843.1</p>
<p>    Gross premium income  1,159.8    vs    992.6</p>
<p>    Underwriting profit	70.7    vs    74.0</p>
<p>    Investment income	 120.6    vs    86.1</p>
<p>Div payable: April 18</p>
<p>On register: March 27</p>
<p>Full name: Mutual &amp; Federal Insurance Company Ltd (insurance)</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said about 10 million rand had been set aside for retrenchment packages at its newly acquired Protea Assurance Co Ltd. It said it expected meaningful contribution to profitability in the short to medium term from the acquisition.</p>
<p>It expected investment income to grow at a slower rate during the second half of ht eyear due to a greater investment in equities and a lesser investment in interest-bearing securities.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
